slow bodies enabled). Kondo on four touched code files 0 errors/0 warnings; cljstyle check clean. Fixture oracle statuses remain pending.\n\nRemaining gaps: the fixture gate is not full Zend statement selection. Marks currently cover echo, expression, yield, and semicolon declare only; excluded categories, compound statements and adjacent suppression require implementation and oracle cases. Hoisted function compilation does not preserve a preceding semicolon directive's lexical threshold, and alternate declare syntax/range validation require further work. Callback membership changes and unregistering a currently executing entry need additional tests and potentially corrections; no broad reentry or exception corpus was run. The production linked publication/site-set and include handoff remain unimplemented and were not tested per instruction. Only the test harness derives ticks; other production execution paths need explicit profile integration. No formal PHP oracle comparison or counter discriminator corpus was run in this session. These gaps prevent a parity or landing claim despite 8/8 fixture assertions.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/publication.cljc; rg -n 'site-set|safepoint|derive' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/{publication,linker,compiler}.cljc test/yang/php/antlr/{ticks_test,e2e_harness}.clj\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/publication.cljc; rg -n 'site-set|safepoint|derive' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/{publication,linker,compiler}.cljc test/yang/php/antlr/{ticks_test,e2e_harness}.clj\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.php.antlr.publication\n  \"P6 (docs/design/yang.php.md section 11): a set of compiled PHP units\n   published as linker modules. The ordering, SCC bundling and publish loop\n   are `yang.core.publication`'s; this namespace supplies the PHP hooks: the\n   includes `lower/imported-unit-names` folds, the `lower/module-spec` and\n   `lower/scc-module-specs` emitters, no site set and no binder table (the\n   PHP hook profile is P7).\n\n   A unit is `{:name path :packet p :strict-types b}`, `path` its normalized\n   relative path; the optional class map entry is `{:name \\\"$classmap\\\"\n   :classes {class path} :paths [path ...]}`. Name assertions stay the\n   linker's: this namespace publishes content, it signs nothing.\"\n  (:require\n    [yang.core.publication :as core]\n    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as lower]\n    [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]))\n\n\n(defn- class-map?\n  \"The autoload class map entry of a unit set, `{:name \\\"$classmap\\\" :classes\n   {class path} :paths [path ...]}`: it imports every path it lists, so it\n   publishes last and an unpublished path is refused by name (plan P6 R9).\"\n  [unit]\n  (= lower/classmap-name (:name unit)))\n\n\n(defn- config\n  [publish-fn]\n  {:imported-names (fn [{:keys [name packet], :as unit}]\n                     (if (class-map? unit)\n                       (lower/classmap-paths unit)\n                       (lower/imported-unit-names packet {:path name}))),\n   :module-spec (fn [registry {:keys [name packet strict-types], :as unit} php-address deps]\n                  (if (class-map? unit)\n                    (lower/classmap-spec registry unit php-address deps)\n                    (lower/module-spec registry packet\n                                       {:path name,\n                                        :strict-types strict-types,\n                                        :php-address php-address,\n                                        :deps deps}))),\n   :scc-module-specs lower/scc-module-specs,\n   :site-set nil,\n   :binder-table nil,\n   :refusal-ns \"yang.php\",\n   :publish-fn publish-fn})\n\n\n(defn publication-order\n  \"Dependency-first names, retaining the input order for acyclic units.\n   Cyclic components appear as sorted member vectors in :order, one\n   publication step per SCC. An include edge no unit and no `published`\n   entry supplies is refused `:yang.php/unpublished-import` by name.\"\n  [units published]\n  (core/publication-order (config publish/publish-module!) units published))\n\n\n(defn publish-units!\n  \"Publish `units` into the content store `handle` over the host registry\n   `registry`, `php` pinned at `php-address` and each include outside the\n   set at its address in `published` ({path address}), in\n   `publication-order`. Answers `{:status :ok :addresses {path address}\n   :bundles {bundle-symbol address}}`, or the first refusal:\n   `publication-order`'s before anything is written, else\n   `publish-module!`'s with a string `:unit`.\"\n  ([handle registry php-address units]\n   (publish-units! handle registry php-address units {}))\n  ([handle registry php-address units published]\n   (publish-units! handle registry php-address units published publish/publish-module!))\n  ([handle registry php-address units published publish-fn]\n   (core/publish-units! (config publish-fn) handle registry php-address units published)))\nrg: src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/linker.cljc: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nrg: src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/compiler.cljc: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/publication.cljc:42:   :site-set nil,\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj:12:    [yang.php.antlr.safepoint :as hooks]\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj:14:    [yang.safepoint :as safepoint]\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj:20:    [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj:106:   `[:thrown message]`. `:execution-budget` derives the PHP safepoint hooks\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj:114:                     derived (:envelope (safepoint/derive-envelope projected profile :test/derived))\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj:115:                     tree (nth (:yin/batch derived) (:yin/root derived))]\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj:131:                                           (:image (derive/stack-image (projected)))\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj:134:                                              (derive/register-image (projected))\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj:142:   `:execution-budget` is a count of PHP `:loop` and `:call` safepoints.\"\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj:174:       (let [derived (:envelope (safepoint/derive-envelope\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj:176:             ast (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast (nth (:yin/batch derived) (:yin/root derived)))\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
