{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files | rg 'linked_harness|siteset.cljc|ticks.*prompt'; cat src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc\ntest/yang/php/antlr/linked_harness.cljc\ntest/yang/typescript/antlr/linked_harness.cljc\ntest/yang/python/antlr/linked_harness.cljc\ncollab/yang-php/1794565785000-engineer-p7b-ticks.prompt.md\ncollab/yang-php/1794568493000-engineer-p7b-ticks-f.prompt.md\ncollab/yang-php/1794568287000-engineer-p7b-ticks-e.prompt.md\ncollab/yang-php/1794566777000-engineer-p7b-ticks-b.prompt.md\ncollab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.prompt.md\ncollab/yang-php/1794567570000-architect-ticks-counter-ruling.prompt.md\ncollab/yang-php/1794568084000-engineer-p7b-ticks-d.prompt.md\ncollab/yang-php/1794569052000-engineer-p7b-ticks-g.prompt.md\n(ns yang.python.antlr.siteset\n  \"C4 slice I7 (docs/design/yang.antlr.md 8.5.6, ruling 14): published site\n   sets for imported modules.\n\n   Site marks never enter canonical rows, so a published module tree\n   carries none; they live in the frontend-metadata side table. A module's\n   site set is that side table's `:yang/site` marks for the module tree,\n   sorted (`yang.safepoint/site-set`) and content-addressed. A separate\n   publication record, keyed by the module's manifest address, pins the\n   association: the exact code root (the manifest's `:yin.module/tree`),\n   the frontend revision, the transformation profile and the set's\n   address. The module manifest keeps its schema: a manifest address names\n   code, and a record names a manifest.\n\n   Discovery. The publisher signs a publication entry per module,\n   `{:yang.site/manifest m :yang.site/record record-address ...}`, and\n   indexes it as the datoms `[e :yang.site/envelope env]` and `[e\n   :yang.site/proof proof]` beside its name envelopes (`signed-entry`).\n   A reader `discover`s a manifest's record addresses from the index\n   datoms it loaded, under the principals it declares; only a declared\n   principal's signature makes an entry count. The record and the set are\n   fetched by address and verified against it.\n\n   A consumer under a profile requiring hooks `admit`s an import: it\n   verifies every pin against the published code root and refuses a\n   missing, empty or mismatched set, naming the profile and the set.\n   `stage` then applies a verified set at link time, as the linker\n   composition's `:stage`: it derives the instrumented module `A'` from the\n   published tree alone, bottom-up over the module's guest requirements,\n   and publishes it beside its `:derive` record. An explicitly noninterruptible profile imports the module\n   as published, with none.\"\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [yang.python.antlr.lower :as lower]\n            [yang.safepoint :as safepoint]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n            [yin.vm.linker.sign :as sign]))\n\n\n(def frontend-revision\n  \"The frontend revision the marks are pinned to: it moves with any change\n   to which nodes the Python lowering marks, or how.\"\n  \"yang.python.antlr.lower/sites-1\")\n\n\n(def lowering-profile\n  \"The transformation profile the marks were made under: the module\n   emitter over the linked prelude, marking these kinds.\"\n  {:yang.site/unit :module,\n   :yang.site/prelude :linked,\n   :yang.site/kinds [:call :line :loop]})\n\n\n(def profile-address\n  \"The address the transformation profile is pinned by.\"\n  (jing/segment-key lowering-profile))\n\n\n(defn- medium\n  []\n  :yang.python.antlr/site-set)\n\n\n(defn site-set-of\n  \"`{:root address :tree tree :set [[path mark] ...]}` for the module map\n   AST `ast`: the address of its canonical tree, the tree's rows and its\n   sorted site set.\"\n  [ast]\n  (let [env (encoder/project (encoder/source-envelope\n                               (medium) [:site-set 0] [ast]))\n        tree (nth (:yin/batch env) (:yin/root env))\n        origin (vm/source-origin (:yin/source-medium env)\n                                 (:yin/batch-token env) (:yin/root env))\n        sites (safepoint/sites (:yin/frontend-metadata env) origin (:root tree))]\n    {:root (:root tree), :tree tree, :set (safepoint/site-set sites)}))\n\n\n(defn record\n  \"The publication record associating manifest `manifest` with site set\n   `set-address` over code root `root`.\"\n  [manifest root set-address]\n  {:yang.site/manifest manifest,\n   :yang.site/root root,\n   :yang.site/revision frontend-revision,\n   :yang.site/profile profile-address,\n   :yang.site/set set-address})\n\n\n(defn publish!\n  \"Publish the site set of module `ast` (published at manifest address\n   `manifest`) into `handle`: the set as one blob, then its record. Answers\n   `{:record r :record-address a :set-address s :set [...]}`.\"\n  [handle manifest ast]\n  (let [{:keys [root set]} (site-set-of ast)\n        set-address (jing/materialize! handle (vec set))\n        r (record manifest root set-address)]\n    {:record r,\n     :record-address (jing/materialize! handle r),\n     :set-address set-address,\n     :set set}))\n\n\n(defn- read-at\n  \"The value at `address` in `handle`: `::absent` when the handle holds no\n   bytes for a segment address (the handle is asked with a not-found\n   sentinel, as a byte store is), nil when `address` is no segment address\n   or its bytes do not hash to it, else the value.\"\n  [handle address]\n  (if-not (jing/segment-address? address)\n    nil\n    (let [bs ((:get-bytes-fn handle) address ::absent)]\n      (cond\n        (= ::absent bs) ::absent\n        (nil? bs) ::absent\n        (jing/segment-bytes-match? address bs) (jing/segment-value address bs)\n        :else nil))))\n\n\n(defn- absent?\n  [x]\n  (= ::absent x))\n\n\n(defn- missing\n  \"The stage's report of the absent `address`: first one met, nothing\n   written.\"\n  [address]\n  {:status :missing, :address address})\n\n\n(defn- fetch\n  \"The value at `address` in `handle`, or nil when absent or not its\n   address.\"\n  [handle address]\n  (let [v (read-at handle address)]\n    (when-not (absent? v) v)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Discovery\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn signed-entry\n  \"The publisher `key`'s (`{:seed :public}`) signed publication entry\n   `{:envelope e :proof p}` for the record at `record-address` of the\n   module at `manifest`: what the index carries so a reader discovers the\n   record from the published code.\"\n  [key manifest record-address]\n  (let [env {:yang.site/op :publish,\n             :yang.site/manifest manifest,\n             :yang.site/record record-address,\n             :yin.module/asserted-by (sign/principal (:public key))}]\n    {:envelope env, :proof (sign/sign-envelope (:seed key) env)}))\n\n\n(defn entry-datoms\n  \"The index datoms of the signed entries `signed`, entity ids from 0.\"\n  [signed]\n  (vec (mapcat (fn [e {:keys [envelope proof]}]\n                 [[e :yang.site/envelope envelope]\n                  [e :yang.site/proof proof]])\n               (range) signed)))\n\n\n(defn discover\n  \"The record addresses `datoms` (`[e a v ...]`, a loaded index's) publish\n   for the module at `manifest`, in datom order: the entries whose proof is\n   a valid signature by one of the `publics` (64 hex keys) the reader\n   declares, and no other.\"\n  [datoms publics manifest]\n  (let [proofs (reduce (fn [acc [e a v]]\n                         (cond-> acc\n                           (= a :yang.site/proof) (update e (fnil conj #{}) v)))\n                       {} datoms)]\n    (vec (distinct\n           (keep (fn [[e a env]]\n                   (when (and (= a :yang.site/envelope)\n                              (map? env)\n                              (= :publish (:yang.site/op env))\n                              (= manifest (:yang.site/manifest env)))\n                     (let [ps (get proofs e)\n                           sig (when (= 1 (count ps))\n                                 (:yin.module/signature (first ps)))]\n                       (when (and (string? sig)\n                                  (some #(sign/verify-envelope\n                                           % (jing/canonical-bytes env) sig)\n                                        publics))\n                         (:yang.site/record env)))))\n                 datoms)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Verification and admission\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- refusal\n  [reason requirement message data]\n  (merge {:status :refused,\n          :reason reason,\n          :profile (:profile requirement),\n          :message (str \"profile \" (pr-str (:profile requirement))\n                        \" requires hooks: \" message)}\n         data))\n\n\n(defn- entry-ok?\n  \"A set entry is `[path mark]`, a path vector and a mark of the profile's\n   kinds (a kind, or `[kind datum ...]`).\"\n  [entry]\n  (and (vector? entry)\n       (= 2 (count entry))\n       (vector? (first entry))\n       (let [mark (second entry)]\n         (boolean (some #{(if (vector? mark) (first mark) mark)}\n                        (:yang.site/kinds lowering-profile))))))\n\n\n(defn verify\n  \"Nil when the record at `record-address` verifies as the site set of the\n   module published at `manifest` in `handle`; `{:status :missing :address\n   a}` for the first address (manifest, record, set, in that order) the\n   handle does not hold; else the first defect `{:defect k ...}` (with the\n   record's `:set` address when it names one): the manifest or record not\n   its address, the record naming another manifest, the code root, the\n   frontend revision or the profile not the published ones, the set not its\n   address or empty, or an entry not a path with a mark kind of the\n   profile's.\"\n  [handle manifest record-address]\n  (let [m (read-at handle manifest)\n        r (when-not (absent? m) (read-at handle record-address))\n        set-address (when (map? r) (:yang.site/set r))\n        set (when-not (or (absent? m) (absent? r))\n              (read-at handle set-address))\n        defect (cond\n                 (not (map? m)) {:defect :manifest-absent}\n                 (not (map? r)) {:defect :record-absent}\n                 (not= manifest (:yang.site/manifest r)) {:defect :manifest}\n                 (not= (:yin.module/tree m) (:yang.site/root r)) {:defect :root}\n                 (not= frontend-revision (:yang.site/revision r))\n                 {:defect :revision}\n                 (not= profile-address (:yang.site/profile r)) {:defect :profile}\n                 (not (vector? set)) {:defect :set-absent}\n                 (empty? set) {:defect :set-empty}\n                 (not (every? entry-ok? set)) {:defect :kind}\n                 :else nil)]\n    (cond\n      (absent? m) (missing manifest)\n      (absent? r) (missing record-address)\n      (absent? set) (missing set-address)\n      defect (cond-> defect set-address (assoc :set set-address)))))\n\n\n(defn admit\n  \"A consumer's decision for the import of the module at `manifest` in\n   `handle`, `record-addresses` the publication records it discovered for\n   it, under `requirement`: `{:profile name :hooks true}` or `{:profile\n   name :noninterruptible true}`. Answers `{:status :ok :instrumented? true\n   :set [...] :set-address s :record a}` when a record verifies, `{:status\n   :ok :instrumented? false :note ...}` for a noninterruptible profile,\n   else a refusal naming the profile and the missing or mismatched set (its\n   address when the record names one); or `{:status :missing :address a}`,\n   the first address a record's verification reads that `handle` does not\n   hold (`verify`).\"\n  [handle manifest record-addresses requirement]\n  (cond\n    (:noninterruptible requirement)\n    {:status :ok,\n     :instrumented? false,\n     :note (str \"profile \" (pr-str (:profile requirement))\n                \" is noninterruptible: imported without a site set\")}\n\n    (:hooks requirement)\n    (if (empty? record-addresses)\n      (refusal :yang.python.antlr/missing-site-set requirement\n               \"no published site set for the module\" {:manifest manifest})\n      (loop [todo record-addresses\n             first-defect nil]\n        (if-let [a (first todo)]\n          (let [v (verify handle manifest a)]\n            (cond\n              (nil? v)\n              (let [set-address (:yang.site/set (fetch handle a))]\n                {:status :ok,\n                 :instrumented? true,\n                 :record a,\n                 :set-address set-address,\n                 :set (fetch handle set-address)})\n\n              (= :missing (:status v)) v\n\n              :else (recur (rest todo) (or first-defect [a v]))))\n          (let [[a defect] first-defect]\n            (refusal :yang.python.antlr/site-set-mismatch requirement\n                     (str \"the published site set\"\n                          (when-let [s (:set defect)] (str \" \" s))\n                          \" does not verify (\" (name (:defect defect)) \")\")\n                     (assoc defect :manifest manifest :record a))))))\n\n    :else\n    (refusal :yang.python.antlr/profile-undeclared requirement\n             \"the profile declares neither :hooks nor :noninterruptible\"\n             {:manifest manifest})))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Link-time application\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- load-tree\n  \"The canonical row set `{:root :rows}` of the tree at `root` in `handle`,\n   every row fetched by its address, depth-first: `{:status :missing\n   :address a}` for the first row the handle does not hold, nil when a row\n   is not its address or no tree row.\"\n  [handle root]\n  (loop [todo [root]\n         rows {}]\n    (if-let [id (peek todo)]\n      (if (contains? rows id)\n        (recur (pop todo) rows)\n        (let [body (read-at handle id)\n              slots (when (vector? body)\n                      (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar (first body)))]\n          (cond\n            (absent? body) (missing id)\n            slots (recur (into (pop todo)\n                               (mapcat (fn [[_ kind] v]\n                                         (case kind\n                                           :node [v]\n                                           :nodes v\n                                           nil))\n                                       slots\n                                       (rest body)))\n                         (assoc rows id (into [id] body)))\n            :else nil)))\n      {:root root, :rows rows})))\n\n\n(defn- derive-module\n  \"Publish into `handle` the instrumented module `A'` of the module `m` at\n   `manifest` for the verified set of `adm`: the published tree with the\n   hooks of `(:hooks-profile requirement)` at its sites, requiring\n   `(:pysp requirement)` beside its own requirements, each guest\n   requirement rebound through `derived` ({A A'}). The `:derive` record\n   (`yang.safepoint/derive-record`) is materialized beside it and its\n   address answered as `:derivation`; nothing transacts it into a ledger.\n   Answers `{:status :ok :address a' :derivation d}`, a refusal, or\n   `{:status :missing :address a}` for the first tree row the handle does\n   not hold, before anything is written.\"\n  [handle registry manifest m adm requirement derived]\n  (let [fail (fn [message data]\n               (refusal :yang.python.antlr/instrumentation-failed requirement\n                        message (assoc data :manifest manifest)))]\n    (if-not (jing/segment-address? (:pysp requirement))\n      (fail \"the hook module is not published\" {})\n      (try\n        (let [tree (load-tree handle (:yin.module/tree m))\n              absent (= :missing (:status tree))\n              sites (into {} (:set adm))\n              inserted (when (and tree (not absent))\n                         (safepoint/insert tree sites\n                                           (:hooks-profile requirement)))\n              ast (when inserted\n                    (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast (:tree inserted)))\n              runtime (or (:runtime requirement) '#{py pysp yang.call})\n              out (when ast\n                    (publish/publish-module!\n                      handle\n                      {:name (:yin.module/name m),\n                       :ast ast,\n                       :exports (:yin.module/exports m),\n                       :requires (assoc (into {}\n                                              (map (fn [[n a]]\n                                                     [n (if (contains? runtime n)\n                                                          a\n                                                          (get derived a a))]))\n                                              (:yin.module/requires m))\n                                        'pysp (:pysp requirement)),\n                       :primitives (into {}\n                                         (map (fn [[n _]]\n                                                [n (lower/primitive-declaration\n                                                     registry n)]))\n                                         (:yin.module/primitives m))}))]\n          (cond\n            absent tree\n            (nil? tree) (fail \"the module's tree is not published\" {})\n            (= :refused (:status out))\n            (fail \"the instrumented module did not publish\" {:cause out})\n            :else\n            {:status :ok,\n             :address (:address out),\n             :instrumented? true,\n             :set-address (:set-address adm),\n             :derivation (jing/materialize!\n                           handle\n                           (safepoint/derive-record\n                             (:yin.module/tree m)\n                             (:yin.module/tree (:manifest out))\n                             (:hooks-profile requirement)\n                             (:sites inserted)))}))\n        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n          (fail (str \"the instrumented module did not derive: \" (ex-message e))\n                {}))))))\n\n\n(defn- records-for\n  \"The record addresses for `manifest`: the local map `records`'s, then\n   those `ctx`'s loaded index datoms publish under its principals.\"\n  [ctx records manifest]\n  (into (vec (get records manifest))\n        (discover (:datoms ctx) (:principals ctx) manifest)))\n\n\n(defn- derive-closure\n  \"The instrumented module of `manifest` under a hook profile, derived\n   bottom-up: each guest requirement is admitted and derived first, so the\n   derived module pins the derived requirements it will link (`derived`,\n   {A A'}, derives a shared requirement once). Answers `{:status :ok\n   :address a' :derivation d :derived derived}`, the first refusal, with\n   `:name` the requirement that was refused and `:via` the module that\n   required it, or `{:status :missing :address a}` for the first address\n   (record, set, guest manifest, tree row) read in a fixed depth-first\n   order that the handle does not hold. Nothing is written until every\n   read has succeeded.\"\n  [ctx registry records requirement manifest derived]\n  (let [handle (:store ctx)\n        runtime (or (:runtime requirement) '#{py pysp yang.call})\n        adm (admit handle manifest (records-for ctx records manifest)\n                   requirement)]\n    (if (not= :ok (:status adm))\n      adm\n      (let [m (fetch handle manifest)\n            deps (sort-by (comp str key)\n                          (remove (comp runtime key)\n                                  (:yin.module/requires m)))\n            below (reduce (fn [acc [n a]]\n                            (if (contains? (:derived acc) a)\n                              acc\n                              (let [r (derive-closure ctx registry records\n                                                      requirement a\n                                                      (:derived acc))]\n                                (case (:status r)\n                                  :ok (assoc acc :derived (:derived r))\n                                  :missing (reduced r)\n                                  (reduced (cond-> (assoc r :via manifest)\n                                             (nil? (:name r)) (assoc :name n)))))))\n                          {:derived derived}\n                          deps)]\n        (if (:status below)\n          below\n          (let [out (derive-module handle registry manifest m adm requirement\n                                   (:derived below))]\n            (if (not= :ok (:status out))\n              out\n              (assoc out :derived (assoc (:derived below) manifest\n                                         (:address out))))))))))\n\n\n(defn- overlay\n  \"A write-buffering handle over `base`: reads see the buffer first, then\n   `base`; puts land in the buffer only, in put order. `flush!` writes the\n   buffer to `base`; dropping the overlay writes nothing.\"\n  [base]\n  (let [buf (atom {:bytes {}, :order []})\n        sentinel #?(:cljs (js-obj)\n                    :default (Object.))]\n    {:handle (assoc base\n                    :get-bytes-fn (fn [address not-found]\n                                    (let [bs (get-in @buf [:bytes address])]\n                                      (if (nil? bs)\n                                        ((:get-bytes-fn base) address not-found)\n                                        bs)))\n                    :put-bytes-fn (fn [address bs]\n                                    (if (or (contains? (:bytes @buf) address)\n                                            (let [existing ((:get-bytes-fn base)\n                                                            address\n                                                            sentinel)]\n                                              (and (some? existing)\n                                                   (not (identical? sentinel\n                                                                    existing)))))\n                                      :present\n                                      (do (swap! buf (fn [b]\n                                                       (-> b\n                                                           (assoc-in [:bytes address]\n                                                                     bs)\n                                                           (update :order conj\n                                                                   address))))\n                                          :inserted))))\n     :flush! (fn []\n               (let [{:keys [bytes order]} @buf]\n                 (doseq [a order] ((:put-bytes-fn base) a (get bytes a)))))}))\n\n\n(def reasons\n  \"The refusal reasons the stage answers, the composition's own.\"\n  #{:yang.python.antlr/missing-site-set\n    :yang.python.antlr/site-set-mismatch\n    :yang.python.antlr/profile-undeclared\n    :yang.python.antlr/instrumentation-failed})\n\n\n(defn stage\n  \"The link-time stage (`yin.vm.linker.interpreter/composition`'s `:stage`)\n   of a Python import under `requirement`: `{:profile name :hooks true\n   :hooks-profile p :pysp address}` or `{:profile name :noninterruptible\n   true}`, with `:runtime` the names of the runtime modules (default `py`,\n   `pysp`, and `yang.call`) it passes through. `yang.call` is the shared\n   call dispatcher, not guest Python code, so it has no Python site marks.\n   `records` ({manifest [record-address ...]})\n   are the local publication's records; a DHT source supplies none and the\n   stage discovers them from the index datoms of its context. The stage\n   reads only the context's `:store` and never fetches: it answers\n   `{:status :missing :address a}` for the first address that store does\n   not hold, and is run again once it is there. Answers\n   `(fn [ctx name address])`: `{:status :ok :address address}` as published\n   when noninterruptible, else the address of the instrumented module\n   derived bottom-up from the verified sets (`:derivation` its `:derive`\n   record's address), or the refusal naming the profile, the set and the\n   `:name` refused.\"\n  [registry requirement records]\n  (let [runtime (or (:runtime requirement) '#{py pysp yang.call})]\n    (fn [ctx name address]\n      (cond\n        (contains? runtime name) {:status :ok, :address address}\n\n        (:noninterruptible requirement)\n        (assoc (admit (:store ctx) address [] requirement) :address address)\n\n        :else\n        (let [{:keys [handle flush!]} (overlay (:store ctx))\n              r (derive-closure (assoc ctx :store handle) registry records\n                                requirement address {})]\n          (case (:status r)\n            :ok (do (flush!)\n                    (select-keys r [:status :address :derivation :instrumented?\n                                    :set-address]))\n            :missing (select-keys r [:status :address])\n            (cond-> r (nil? (:name r)) (assoc :name name))))))))\n\n\n(defn signed-entries\n  \"The `publisher` key's signed publication entries for the site sets\n   `publish-units!` answered: `sites` (`:sites`), the manifest of each\n   from `addresses` (a Python name) or `bundles` (a bundle symbol), in\n   key order. The publisher that asserts these names indexes them in the\n   same transaction (`entry-datoms`); a module with no entry is refused\n   by every hook-profile reader.\"\n  [publisher sites addresses bundles]\n  (mapv (fn [[k s]]\n          (signed-entry publisher (or (get addresses k) (get bundles k))\n                        (:record-address s)))\n        (sort-by (comp str key) sites)))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The existing publication path confirms the main gap: it explicitly publishes no site set, while the Python linker has a verified site-set and derivation pipeline that can inform the PHP implementation. I’m checking how PHP’s module dependencies and bundled aliases fit that pipeline before changing it."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/yang/php/antlr/linked_harness.cljc; cat src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc; rg -n 'module-spec|scc-module-specs|primitive-declaration' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc; rg -n 'site.set|site-set|handoff' collab/orch-lane/1794700000000-architect-safepoint-slice3-design.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/yang/php/antlr/linked_harness.cljc; cat src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc; rg -n 'module-spec|scc-module-specs|primitive-declaration' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc; rg -n 'site.set|site-set|handoff' collab/orch-lane/1794700000000-architect-safepoint-slice3-design.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.php.antlr.linked-harness\n  \"The linked profile's composition for the PHP tests (P6, docs/design/\n   yang.php.md section 11): the namespace that requires this is the\n   publisher of `php`, so it publishes the module once per process into one\n   in-memory content store, publishes a fixture's non-entry units beside it\n   bottom-up, and serves them to the entry unit's run over a\n   `yin.vm.linker.interpreter` composition under `:trusted` derivation.\n\n   A linked run builds the entry unit's task on one of the three vector VMs\n   with a link pair, then runs the VM and serves the pair alternately until\n   the VM stops blocking, as the REPL's drive does. The AST walker is not a\n   backend here: its link of `php` is refused until L-b.\"\n  (:require\n    [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n    [yang.core.call :as call]\n    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as lower]\n    [yang.php.antlr.portable-harness :as portable]\n    [yang.php.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n    [yang.php.antlr.publication :as publication]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n    [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n    [yin.vm.linker.interpreter :as link]\n    [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n    [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n    [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\n    [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as sr-linearize]\n    [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n\n(defn registry\n  \"The host registry a linked PHP composition registers: the `require`\n   handlers, then `cell`, `data` and `integer` under the portable limits.\"\n  []\n  (portable/linked-registry))\n\n\n(def published\n  \"`yang.call` and `php` published once into their own content store.\"\n  (delay\n    (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n          call-result (publish/publish-module! store (call/module-spec (registry)))\n          result (publish/publish-module! store (prelude/module-spec (registry)\n                                                                     (:address call-result)))]\n      {:store store,\n       :result result,\n       :address (:address result),\n       :call-address (:address call-result)})))\n\n\n(defn publish-units!\n  \"`units` (`[{:name path :packet p :strict-types b}]`) published into\n   `php`'s own content store, where its pinned requirement already lives:\n   `publication/publish-units!`'s answer.\"\n  [units]\n  (publication/publish-units! (:store @published) (registry) (:address @published) units))\n\n\n(defn source\n  \"The serving composition over the published store: `name-env` names `php`\n   and each published module, derivation `:trusted`, the test being the\n   publisher.\"\n  [name-env]\n  (link/composition {:content-store (:store @published),\n                     :name-env (merge {'php (:address @published),\n                                       'yang.call (:call-address @published)} name-env),\n                     :derivation :trusted}))\n\n\n(def backends\n  \"Each vector backend's root task over a program AST and composition.\"\n  {:semantic (fn [ast opts]\n               (semantic/load-ast (semantic/create-vm opts)\n                                  (vm/ast->datoms ast)\n                                  vm/ast-contract)),\n   :stack (fn [ast opts]\n            (dvm/create-vm (:image (derive/stack-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast))))\n                           (assoc opts :contract vm/stack-contract))),\n   :register (fn [ast opts]\n               (rvm/create-vm (derive/register-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast)))\n                              (assoc opts :contract vm/register-contract)))})\n\n\n(defn composition\n  \"A task's composition over `modules` and the link `pair`.\"\n  [modules pair]\n  {:make-stream tu/make-stream,\n   :capability-secret tu/secret,\n   :secret-source (fn [origin] (str tu/secret \"/\" (name origin))),\n   :primitives vm/primitives,\n   :modules modules,\n   :link-request (:requests pair),\n   :link-response (:responses pair)})\n\n\n(defn drive\n  \"Run `task` and serve `pair` from `src` alternately until the task stops\n   blocking, at most 80 rounds. Returns `[task pair]`.\"\n  [task pair src]\n  (loop [task (vm/run task)\n         pair pair\n         i 0]\n    (if (and (vm/blocked? task) (< i 80))\n      (let [pair (:pair (link/serve {:pair pair, :source src}))]\n        (recur (vm/run task) pair (inc i)))\n      [task pair])))\n\n\n(defn run-linked\n  \"The finished task of the linked program `ast` on `backend`, served from\n   `src`. A refused link surfaces as the program's own diagnostics.\"\n  [backend ast src]\n  (let [pair (link/make-pair)\n        task ((get backends backend) ast (composition (registry) pair))]\n    (first (drive task pair src))))\n\n\n(defn name-env\n  \"The name environment naming every published module of `result`\n   (`publish-units!`'s answer): module symbol to address.\"\n  [result]\n  (merge (into {} (map (fn [[path address]] [(lower/path-module-symbol path) address]))\n               (:addresses result))\n         (:bundles result)))\n\n\n(defn run-fixture\n  \"`{backend value}` for the multi-unit fixture `units` (`{path packet}`,\n   the entry unit `main`, default `lower/entry-path`) on the three vector\n   VMs: the non-entry units are published bottom-up, the entry unit\n   lowered `:linked` and run. `value` is `run-main`'s map.\"\n  ([units] (run-fixture units lower/entry-path {}))\n  ([units main opts]\n   (let [entry (get units main)\n         others (cond-> (mapv (fn [[path packet]] {:name path, :packet packet})\n                              (dissoc units main))\n                  (:class-map opts) (conj (assoc (:class-map opts) :name lower/classmap-name)))\n         result (publish-units! others)]\n     (when-not (= :ok (:status result))\n       (throw (ex-info \"fixture units failed to publish\" {:result result})))\n     (let [{:keys [ast warnings]}\n           (lower/lower-program entry\n                                (cond-> (merge {:prelude :linked,\n                                                :path main,\n                                                :paths (when (:computed? opts) (keys (:addresses result)))}\n                                               (dissoc opts :computed? :src :request))\n                                  (:class-map opts) (assoc :class-map true)\n                                  (some? (:request opts)) (assoc :request-node\n                                                                 (portable/request-node (:request opts)))))\n           src (or (:src opts) (source (name-env result)))]\n       {:warnings warnings,\n        :values (into {}\n                      (map (fn [k] [k (vm/value (run-linked k ast src))]))\n                      (keys backends))}))))\n(ns yang.php.antlr.safepoint\n  \"The PHP `:loop` and `:call` hooks. A bounded run charges one safepoint to\n   its per-run counter; exhaustion unwinds past guest handlers and raises the\n   operational fatal, not a guest Throwable.\"\n  (:require\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]))\n\n\n(def profile\n  {:loop 'php.sp/loop, :call {:hook 'php.sp/call, :sequence true}})\n\n\n(def ticks-profile\n  \"Statement completion hooks for PHP's lexical ticks directives. This is\n   separate from the execution-budget profile so ticks do not charge it.\"\n  {:line {:hook 'php.sp/line, :operands true, :after true}})\n\n\n(def fatal-text\n  \"Maximum execution time of 30 seconds exceeded\")\n\n\n(def ^:private function-definitions\n  '[[php.sp/exhaust!\n     ;; the terminal root escape: guest handlers, returns and finalizers\n     ;; cannot replace the operational fatal\n     (fn []\n       (php/root-fatal \"Maximum execution time of 30 seconds exceeded\"))]\n    [php.sp/tick\n     (fn []\n       (let [n (cell/get php.sp/remaining)]\n         (if (= n 0)\n           (php.sp/exhaust!)\n           (do (cell/set! php.sp/remaining (- n 1)) :php/null))))]\n    [php.sp/loop (fn [] (php.sp/tick))]\n    [php.sp/call (fn [] (php.sp/tick))]])\n\n\n(defn- definitions->uast\n  [defs]\n  (u/seq-nodes (map (fn [[k form]] (u/def! k (u/sexp->uast form))) defs)))\n\n\n(defn program\n  \"The bounded run: hook definitions and a counter holding `budget`, then the\n   safepoint-derived program `ast`. `budget` must be a non-negative integer;\n   anything else is a named host-side error, not a guest diagnostic.\"\n  [budget ast]\n  (when-not (and (integer? budget) (not (neg? budget)))\n    (throw (ex-info \"php.sp/remaining budget must be a non-negative integer\"\n                    {:yang.php.antlr.safepoint/error :invalid-budget\n                     :budget budget})))\n  (u/mark-tails\n    (u/then (definitions->uast function-definitions)\n            (u/then (u/def! 'php.sp/remaining (u/sexp->uast (list 'cell/new budget)))\n                    ast))))\n3911:(defn module-spec\n3918:  (core-module/module-spec\n3975:  (core-module/module-spec\n3985:(defn scc-module-specs\n4027:        bundle (core-module/module-spec\n4036:    (core-module/scc-module-specs\n16:I’ve confirmed that include units need an explicit site-set handoff: canonical published rows carry no marks. I’ll make that a landing requirement for PHP, alongside a small profile option for hooks that run after normal statement completion. Python will keep its existing hook-before behavior, and neither path needs a VM semantic change.\n124:| Eval unit, P9 | A new compilation produces its own source occurrence, site set, and derivation under the run’s selected profile. Caller scope sharing does not substitute caller locations. Until P9, preserve the existing unsupported result. |\n138:| Published source association | Content-addressed occurrence site set, bound to the exact canonical root and frontend/profile revision |\n140:| Derivation record | Input/output roots, complete hook profile—including `:after`—and selected-site-set address |\n145:A published canonical tree alone cannot recover marks. Python addresses this through published site sets and link-time derivation: [yang.antlr.md:3040](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yang.antlr.md:3040). **PHP does not yet publish them**—its publication configuration explicitly sets `:site-set nil`: [publication.cljc:41](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/publication.cljc:41).\n149:- Publish and retrieve verified site sets for included guest code.\n156:**Stripping rule:** omit `:line` from the profile to derive an executable without line hooks. Never delete inserted calls from an already derived image. A compact execution package may omit side tables after derivation, provided its pinned provenance remains retrievable. A package intended for later instrumentation must retain/retrieve its site set.\n172:Derivation traverses the program and recomputes tail marks; sorted site-set construction adds sorting work. Bundle growth includes wrappers, operands, changed ancestors, and tail-mark changes. Content addressing shares identical rows, so these occurrence counts are not byte estimates. Measure rows and serialized bytes in acceptance.\n256:| 5 | Publication/linker integration seat | Enable the existing publication `:site-set` seam in PHP; add a PHP site-set adapter, verified link-time derivation, hook dependency pins, and SCC alias rebinding. Extend include and portable publication fixtures. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '3900,4050p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc; rg -n 'php.sp/line|module-spec|primitive-declaration' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/{prelude,lower}.cljc; cat deps.edn | head -80; cat docs/agents/build-n-test.md | head -100\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '3900,4050p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc; rg -n 'php.sp/line|module-spec|primitive-declaration' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/{prelude,lower}.cljc; cat deps.edn | head -80; cat docs/agents/build-n-test.md | head -100\"","aggregated_output":"   scope arrives as arguments (P6 S3 gives them meaning; S2 includes only\n   at an entry unit's top level, whose variables are the globals).\"\n  [packet {:keys [path strict-types]}]\n  (let [ctx (assoc (context packet {:path path, :linked? true}) :module? true)\n        defs [(u/def! 'spec (u/lit {:path path, :strict-types (if strict-types 1 0)}))\n              (u/def! 'body (u/lam ['%scope '%ctx] (unit-node ctx true)))]\n        operands (into [(core-module/require-node prelude/module-name)] defs)\n        params (mapv (fn [i] (symbol (str \"%d\" i))) (range (count operands)))]\n    (u/mark-tails (apply u/app (u/lam params (u/lit nil)) operands))))\n\n\n(defn module-spec\n  \"`yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-module!`'s spec for the unit at `path` over\n   the host registry `registry`, requiring `php` at `php-address` and each\n   included unit at its address in `deps` ({path address}). A free name no\n   requirement or profile supplies is refused before anything is published.\n   This namespace emits; it never publishes.\"\n  [registry packet {:keys [path strict-types php-address deps]}]\n  (core-module/module-spec\n    :yang.php/refusal :yang.php/undeclared-free registry\n    {:name (path-module-symbol path),\n     :ast (module-packet packet {:path path, :strict-types strict-types}),\n     :exports module-exports,\n     :runtime-name prelude/module-name,\n     :runtime-address php-address,\n     :deps (into {} (map (fn [[p a]] [(path-module-symbol p) a])) deps)}))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The autoload class map (plan P6 R9)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def classmap-exports\n  \"The exports of the class map module: the lower-cased class name to path\n   map, and the path to delivery-thunk map the computed include resolves\n   through.\"\n  '#{classes paths})\n\n\n(defn classmap-paths\n  \"The literal paths a class map `{:classes {class path} :paths [path ...]}`\n   publishes thunks for: `:paths`, else the class map's values, and always the\n   class map's values. Normalized, sorted, distinct.\"\n  [{:keys [classes paths]}]\n  (vec (sort (distinct (map #(let [r (normalize-unit-path %)]\n                               (when (:error r) (throw (ex-info \"unmappable class map path\"\n                                                                {:yang.php/diagnostic :yang.php/unsupported,\n                                                                 :construct (:error r), :path %})))\n                               (:path r))\n                            (concat (vals classes) paths))))))\n\n\n(defn classmap-packet\n  \"The class map as one linker module (the unit module shape): `classes`\n   maps each lower-cased class name to its normalized path, `paths` each\n   listed path to its delivery thunk.\"\n  [{:keys [classes] :as cm}]\n  (let [paths (classmap-paths cm)\n        norm (fn [p] (:path (normalize-unit-path p)))\n        defs [(u/def! 'classes\n                      (u/lit (into {} (map (fn [[c p]] [(str/lower-case c) (norm p)])) classes)))\n              (u/def! 'paths\n                      (reduce (fn [m p] (app* 'assoc m (u/lit p) (delivery-thunk p)))\n                              (u/lit {})\n                              paths))]\n        operands (into [(core-module/require-node prelude/module-name)] defs)\n        params (mapv (fn [i] (symbol (str \"%d\" i))) (range (count operands)))]\n    (u/mark-tails (apply u/app (u/lam params (u/lit nil)) operands))))\n\n\n(defn classmap-spec\n  \"`publish-module!`'s spec for the class map `cm` over the host registry\n   `registry`, `php` at `php-address` and each listed path's module at its\n   address in `deps` ({path address}).\"\n  [registry cm php-address deps]\n  (core-module/module-spec\n    :yang.php/refusal :yang.php/undeclared-free registry\n    {:name classmap-module,\n     :ast (classmap-packet cm),\n     :exports classmap-exports,\n     :runtime-name prelude/module-name,\n     :runtime-address php-address,\n     :deps (into {} (map (fn [[p a]] [(path-module-symbol p) a])) deps)}))\n\n\n(defn scc-module-specs\n  \"The SCC publication shape for a mutual include group: sorted members,\n   indexed exports m0-spec/m0-body, one `phpscc.<members>` bundle followed\n   by the thin member aliases. Internal deliveries answer `{:status :ok}`\n   and read the bundle's own bodies; only `php` and outgoing includes are\n   pinned. `units` are `[{:name path :packet p :strict-types b}]`.\"\n  [registry units php-address deps]\n  (let [units (vec (sort-by :name units))\n        deps (apply dissoc deps (map :name units))\n        bundle-name (symbol (str \"phpscc.\"\n                                 (str/join \"+\" (map #(str/replace (str (path-module-symbol (:name %))) #\"^phpm\\.\" \"\")\n                                                    units))))\n        keys-for (into {} (map-indexed (fn [i unit]\n                                         [(:name unit) [(symbol (str \"m\" i \"-spec\"))\n                                                        (symbol (str \"m\" i \"-body\"))]])\n                                       units))\n        internal-names (into {} (map (fn [nm] [(path-module-symbol nm) nm])) (keys keys-for))\n        internal (set (keys internal-names))\n        rewrite (fn [node]\n                  (cond\n                    (and (= :variable (:type node))\n                         (symbol? (:name node))\n                         (some? (namespace (:name node)))\n                         (contains? internal (symbol (namespace (:name node))))\n                         (= \"body\" (name (:name node))))\n                    (u/v (second (get keys-for (get internal-names (symbol (namespace (:name node)))))))\n                    (and (= :application (:type node))\n                         (= 'try-require (get-in node [:operator :name]))\n                         (contains? internal (get-in node [:operands 0 :value])))\n                    (u/lit {:status :ok})\n                    :else node))\n        spec-defs (mapv (fn [{:keys [name strict-types]}]\n                          (u/def! (first (get keys-for name))\n                                  (u/lit {:path name, :strict-types (if strict-types 1 0)})))\n                        units)\n        body-defs (mapv (fn [{:keys [name packet]}]\n                          (let [ctx (context packet {:path name, :linked? true})]\n                            (u/def! (second (get keys-for name))\n                                    (u/lam ['%scope '%ctx]\n                                           (walk/postwalk rewrite (unit-node ctx true))))))\n                        units)\n        ast (core-module/module-tree (concat spec-defs body-defs [(core-module/require-node prelude/module-name)]))\n        bundle (core-module/module-spec\n                 :yang.php/refusal :yang.php/undeclared-free registry\n                 {:name bundle-name,\n                  :ast ast,\n                  :exports (set (mapcat val keys-for)),\n                  :runtime-name prelude/module-name,\n                  :runtime-address php-address,\n                  :deps (into {} (map (fn [[p a]] [(path-module-symbol p) a])) deps)})\n        require-profile (vm/profile-of vm/primitives 'require)]\n    (core-module/scc-module-specs\n      bundle\n      (mapv (fn [{:keys [name]}]\n              (let [[sk bk] (get keys-for name)]\n                (core-module/alias-spec (path-module-symbol name) module-exports\n                                        require-profile bundle-name sk bk)))\n            units))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The lowering stage\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def program-medium\n  \"The program medium's logical identity when the composition names none.\"\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3911:(defn module-spec\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3918:  (core-module/module-spec\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3975:  (core-module/module-spec\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3985:(defn scc-module-specs\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:4027:        bundle (core-module/module-spec\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:4036:    (core-module/scc-module-specs\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:4498:    [php.sp/line\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:6306:(defn module-spec\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:6312:  (core/module-spec {:module-name module-name,\n{:deps {org.clojure/core.async {:mvn/version \"1.8.741\"}\n        org.clojure/tools.reader {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ring/ring {:mvn/version \"1.14.1\"}\n        com.cognitect/transit-clj {:mvn/version \"1.0.333\"}\n        org.replikativ/boring {:mvn/version \"0.1.30\"}\n        com.datomic/peer {:mvn/version \"1.0.7364\"}\n        org.postgresql/postgresql {:mvn/version \"42.7.3\"}\n        org.clojure/data.json {:mvn/version \"2.5.0\"}\n        http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}\n        org.jsoup/jsoup {:mvn/version \"1.18.3\"}\n        instaparse/instaparse {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ;; yang.python.antlr: the runtime the generated Python3 parser runs\n        ;; on; pinned to the tool version in :antlr-gen (they are one release)\n        org.antlr/antlr4-runtime {:mvn/version \"4.13.2\"}\n        criterium/criterium {:mvn/version \"0.4.6\"}\n        io.github.rctcwyvrn/blake3 {:mvn/version \"1.3\"}\n        stigmergy/chp {:mvn/version \"0.1.0-SNAPSHOT\"\n                       :exclusions [refactor-nrepl/refactor-nrepl]}}\n :cljd/opts {}\n ;; build/antlr/python3/classes: the generated Python3 parser, produced by\n ;; `clj -M:antlr-gen` (antlr/python3/manifest.edn); absent until generated\n :paths [\"src/clj\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/cljs\" \"src/cljd\"\n         \"build/antlr/python3/classes\" \"build/antlr/php/classes\"\n         \"build/antlr/typescript/classes\"]\n :aliases {:clean {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                   :exec-fn clean/clean}\n           :profile-btree {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                           :extra-deps {persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                                        {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                           :main-opts [\"-m\" \"btree-bench\"]}\n           :test {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :extra-deps {io.github.cognitect-labs/test-runner\n                               {:git/tag \"v0.5.1\" :git/sha \"dfb30dd\"}\n                               ;; latte-kernel: the LaTTe proof assistant's kernel,\n                               ;; the differential oracle for the yang.clojure gap\n                               ;; program (pinned; MIT; dependency-free)\n                               latte-kernel/latte-kernel\n                               {:git/url \"https://github.com/latte-central/latte-kernel\"\n                                :git/sha \"86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279\"}}\n                  ;; The guest recursion limit allows depth that needs more than the\n                  ;; JVM's platform default thread stack (1024 KB on Linux, 2048 KB on\n                  ;; macOS): under 1 MB the guard loses to a JVM StackOverflowError\n                  ;; before it can raise Python's RecursionError, so the same tests\n                  ;; pass on macOS and fail on Linux. 4 MB is twice the measured\n                  ;; macOS-default minimum, leaving headroom as the prelude grows.\n                  ;; Evidence: docs/agents/known-gaps.md (the recursion rows).\n                  ;; merged stack policy: -Xss64m supersedes the earlier -Xss4m —\n                  ;; deep assertion payloads (the PHPT selection diagnostics and\n                  ;; the conformance compositions) overflow smaller stacks in\n                  ;; clojure.test's printer on shiva (verified green at -Xss64m;\n                  ;; the 4m minimum for the prelude recursion rows still holds)\n                  :jvm-opts [\"-Xss64m\"]\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cognitect.test-runner\"]\n                  :exec-fn cognitect.test-runner.api/test}\n           :nREPL {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                   :extra-deps {nrepl/nrepl {:mvn/version \"1.0.0\"}\n                                cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}}\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"nrepl.cmdline\" \"--middleware\" \"[cider.nrepl/cider-middleware]\"]}\n           :cljs {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\" \"build/antlr/python3/js\" \"build/antlr/php/js\"]\n                  :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                               reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                               com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}}\n           :dev {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                 :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                              cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}\n                              reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                              com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}\n                              ;; benchmark baseline + psset-fixtures\n                              ;; generator only; production uses\n                              ;; dao.data.btree\n                              persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                              {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                 :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]}\n           ;; The one ClojureDart pin. Compose it with the build aliases:\n           ;; clj -M:clojuredart:cljd ..., clj -M:clojuredart:cljd-yin-repl-build ...\n           :clojuredart {:extra-deps {sonwh98/clojuredart\n                                      {:git/url \"https://github.com/sonwh98/ClojureDart.git\"\n                                       :sha \"7d00ee2aa7fa9d990581e78ebc4a66b93cb70a31\"}\n                                      }}\n           :cljd {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n---\ndescription: Build, lint, test commands, TDD guidelines, and bracket debugging for Clojure, ClojureScript, Node.js, and ClojureDart\n---\n\n# BUILD & TEST\n\n## Commands\n\n```sh\n# Tests (Babashka runner)\nbb test              # All three lanes (JVM, Node, Dart), fast default form: no slow tests\nbb test:all          # Every test on every lane, slow ones included (JVM takes 20+ min)\nbb test:slow         # Only the slow tests, on every lane\n# One lane alone: <task>:clj, <task>:cljs, <task>:cljd\nbb test:clj          # JVM, fast: skips ^:slow (bare `clj -M:test` runs them too)\nbb test:cljs         # Node (shadow-cljs :cljs alias), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\nbb test:cljd         # Dart (needs flutter on PATH), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\nbb test:all:clj      # JVM, no filter: `clojure -M:test`\nbb test:all:cljs     # Node with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:all:cljd     # Dart with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:slow:clj     # JVM: `-i :slow` (long-loops-test, ~14 min)\nbb test:slow:cljs    # Node: only the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:slow:cljd    # Dart: only those namespaces' generated tests, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\n# Slow tests: tag a deftest ^:slow. The JVM runner then excludes it from `bb test:clj`.\n# Node and Dart have no tag filter, so a .cljc slow test also wraps its body in\n# (dao.test-slow/guard \"name\" (fn [] ...)); it prints SKIP unless DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1.\n# Node and Dart select slow tests by NAMESPACE (derived by grepping `slow/guard`\n# under test/), so the non-slow tests inside those namespaces also run there.\n# On Node, shadow also runs the test namespaces those nine require (about\n# seven more, e.g. lower-portable-test); on Dart only the nine namespaces run.\n# Run test:slow / test:all before a big merge or a commit that touches many parts.\n# Run one Dart lane at a time per machine (the limit is cores and the Flutter cache,\n# not subsystems). On the many-core remote hosts see \"Remote test servers\" below for\n# which lanes may overlap.\n#\n# When to tag a test slow: when it takes more than about 5 s on any lane (the\n# Python e2e tests sit on a ~3 s floor, so their JVM cut is 3.0 s). The\n# default lanes must stay in minutes; 22 JVM tests (0.75% of the suite) were\n# 81% of its test time. Tag it ^:slow on the JVM; if it is a .cljc test, also\n# wrap its body in dao.test-slow/guard so Node and Dart skip it by default. A\n# test that is slow only on Dart (dao.jing.dht-test/unproven-chunks-... takes\n# 72 s there, 3.6 s on the JVM) is a candidate for a speed investigation first.\n# Python slow set (2026-10-06): 65 ^:slow and 15 guard-only tests in the\n# yang.python.antlr e2e, e2e-c1, prelude-parity, safepoint, float-address\n# and int-contract tests; a Python slice landing runs `bb test:sub:clj yang.python --slow`\n# (or `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <ns>`).\n# While iterating, use the Gate Ladder (see below): G0 iterate via `bb test:sub:clj <own>`\n# or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`. Do not run the full `bb test` while iterating.\n# When a test fails, reproduce and fix it by running ONLY the failing test\n# (`clojure -M:test -n <ns> -v <ns>/<var>`, Node `--test=<ns>`, Dart `--only <ns>`) --\n# never the whole suite (owner ruling 2026-11-01; see Gate Ladder G0).\n# Individual tests run fine on the laptop; suite-scale runs (G1 subsystem sets,\n# G2 changed sets, full suites, slow tier, nightly) run on shiva/jupiter --\n# the suite has outgrown the laptop (owner ruling 2026-11-04).\n# At slice checkpoints, run G1 (`bb test:sub <own>`). Before landing a slice, run\n# G2 (`bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes).\n# Full repo-wide `bb test` runs once daily on the remote hosts (04:00 VN);\n# a MERGE needs only the affected tests (bb test:changed) -- owner ruling 2026-11-01;\n# for a fix branch, the previously-failing tests green IS the merge bar\n# (owner ruling 2026-11-07; see Gate Ladder G0).\n# Cross-host bugs show only on Node or Dart, so tri-host verification is mandatory\n# for every gate from G1 upward. Run one lane set at a time per machine to avoid\n# contention (a laptop has 8 cores; the 24- and 48-core remote hosts have room to\n# overlap lanes, see \"Remote test servers\" below).\n# Measured fast-lane times (2026-10-03): bb test about 14 min = JVM 5.5 + Node\n# 3.8 + Dart 4.3, plus builds. test:slow: Node and Dart about 5 min each (mostly\n# compile); the JVM half is estimated at 17 min (long-loops-test alone is 14),\n# not yet run end to end. test:all: JVM 20+ min, also an estimate.\nnpm test             # Node.js tests\n\n# Cross-host peers the JVM lane spawns. `bb test` builds both. A bare\n# `bb test:clj` builds only the Node REPL (it depends on build:yin-repl-node);\n# without build:yin-repl-peer first, the Dart-peer tests skip with a printed notice.\n# Under `bb test:sub` and `bb test:changed`, prerequisites are derived automatically.\nbb build:yin-repl-peer   # Dart exe build/yin-repl-peer (yin.repl R5 pairs)\nbb build:yin-repl-node   # Node REPL target/yin-repl.js; REQUIRED by\n                         # yin.repl.dht-process-test (JVM-to-Node DHT reader,\n                         # and the linker L5 Node reader that requires a module\n                         # by name): `clojure -M:test` without it fails that test\n```\n\n### Changed-only tests: `bb test:changed`\n\n`bb test:changed` (src/dev/affected.clj) runs the fast tests a change can\nreach: the reverse require closure of the files changed since the\nmerge-base with master, plus fixtures that mention a changed resource path,\ntests that walk a changed tree, and each src file's `_test` by convention.\nA walker is a file calling file-seq, fs/glob, fs/list-dir,\nfs/walk-file-tree or .listFiles; each string literal argument of its\nio/file, fs/file, fs/path, fs/glob, java.io.File. or File. calls is a root\n(let-bound roots count), and a change under a root selects it. The three\nlanes run in parallel (logs: target/profile/changed-<lane>.log) after the\nneeded builds. `test:changed:list` shows what and why; `:clj`/`:cljs`/\n`:cljd` run one lane; `--base REF`; `--changed FILE...` (absolute OK; a\ntypo, an empty list or the wrong cwd exits 1). Use it to iterate and to\nland a slice confined to a package. Exit 2 (from :list too) is a wide\nchange (deps.edn bb.edn shadow-cljs.edn mise.toml .cljstyle src/dev/\nantlr/ .clj-kondo/ package*/pubspec*): it runs nothing; run `bb test`,\nas for a change to the core everything requires (yin.vm engine,\ndao.stream, codecs) and before a big merge. Not seen: dynamic loads\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
